Barnes & Noble Discover Great New Writers
For centuries, the story of Dracula has captured the imagination of readers and storytellers alike. Kostova's breathtaking first novel, ten years in the writing, is an accomplished retelling of this ancient tale. "The story that follows is one I never intended to commit to paper.. As an historian, I have learned that, in fact, not everyone who reaches back into history can survive it." With these words, a nameless narrator unfolds a story that began 30 years earlier.
Late one night in 1972, as a 16-year-old girl, she discovers a mysterious book and a sheaf of letters in her father's library -- a discovery that will have dreadful and far-reaching consequences, and will send her on a journey of mind-boggling danger. While seeking clues to the secrets of her father's past and her mother's puzzling disappearance, she follows a trail from London to Istanbul to Budapest and beyond, and learns that the letters in her possession provide a link to one of the world's darkest and most intoxicating figures. Generation after generation, the legend of Dracula has enticed and eluded both historians and opportunists alike. Now a young girl undertakes the same search that ended in the death and defilement of so many others -- in an attempt to save her father from an unspeakable fate.
(Fall 2005 Selection)"�	
�	Bezsm'rtnata semeina saga obkhvashcha period ot chetv'rt vek v nai-novata istoriia na SAShch.
Bratiata Dzhordakh se boriat po svoi nachin za miasto v zhivota. Ediniiat preuspiava s tsenata na neposilni zhertvi, a drugiiat se razplashcha s's sebe si v neprestanna borba s okolnite. Lutaiki se mezhdu bednostta i bogatstvoto, liubovta i omrazata, alchnostta i chestoliubieto geroite t'rsiat trudnoto shchastie v tazi pritcha za s'vremennata tsivilizatsiia.
Tova e istoriiata na bratiata Rudolf i Tomas Dzhordakh i tiakhnata sestra Gretkhen. Bashcha im, germanski emigrant ot 1920 g., srazhaval se na pogreshnata strana prez P'rvata svetovna voina, sega prez 1945 g. raboti v opushena pekarna, k'deto prodava prestoiali chereshovi paiove. Ogorchen, ozloben i neshchasten, Aksel Dzhordakh e chuzhd za detsata i primirenata si s'pruga. Rudi, poslushniiat sin, e umen, tikh i prilezhen. Za nego dobroto obrazovanie e pasport za po-dob'r zhivot. Tom e buen, m'rzeliv i agresiven i ne vizhda po-dalech ot nosa si. Vsichko koeto iska, postiga s iumrutsite si. A Gretkhen, naivna, krasiva i nespokoina, prosto si t'rsi m'zh. Trima mladi khora, vseki umen po svoemu, t'rsiat p'tia si v zhivota. Koi shche postigne uspekh i po kak'v nachin?"�
�Istoriite sa predstaveni kato razkazi na grupa poklonnitsii, p'tuvashchi ot Sautu'rk za Kent'rb'ri za poklonenie v katedralata v Kent'rb'ri. Po-k'sno khram't e razrushen ot Khenri VIII, v dneshni dni na tova miasto e izgradena turisticheska atraktsiia, narechena Kent'rb'riiski razkazi). Chos'r razkazva ot p'rvo litse, kato za s'bitie, v koeto samiiat toi e uchastnik. Za po-goliama avtentichnost v prologa e posochena i data - vtornik, 16 april. Na tozi den v strannopriemnitsata na Khari Beili se s'birat 29 dushi, mezhdu koito i Chos'r, gotveshchi se da otidat na poklonenie. Geroite sa: ritsar, zaedno s's svoia sin - or'zhenosets, melnichar, d'rvodelets, gotvach, pravist, moriak, igumenka, monakh, drug monakh-skitnik, uchen ot Oksford, pastor, prodavach na indulgentsii, lekar, t'rgovets, Franklin (svoboden zemedelski stopanin), burzhoazka ot grad Bat, 5 londonski grazhdani, ikonom, iomen, monakhinia i trima sveshchenosluzhiteli, pridruzhavashchi igumenkata, i Chos'r."�
�Ako ima neshcho, koeto turskiiat student po politologiia Iomer e nauchil za niakolko mesetsa v Bost'n, tova e, che amerikantsite obozhavat da izgovariat imena. Imenata za tiakh sa mostove k'm zam'tsite na choveshkoto s'shchestvuvane i nai-veche chrez tiakh v nego se prom'kvat kakto priiateli, taka i vragove. Nauchavash nechie ime i imash dost'p do polovinata mu s'shchestvuvane. Ostanaloto sa chastichki i podrobnosti. A v Amerika Iomer se prevr'shcha v Omar, za da zazhivee s Abed i Piiu i da se vliubi ludo v Geil.
Geil e privlekatelna amerikanka, koiato v deistvitelnost se kazva Zarpandit, chuvstva se kato chuzhdenka v sobstvenata si strana i prikriva svoiata nesigurnost i sramezhlivost zad neobichaini manii.
Abed se stremi k'm nauchna stepen po biotekhnologii i se trevozhi za vsichko - za Iomer, za neochakvanoto poseshchenie na maika si, za stereotipite za arabite v Amerika i za priiatelkata si, koiato e ostavil v Maroko.
Piiu e ispanets, koito uchi za z'bolekar, v'preki strakha si k'm ostri predmeti, ozadachen ot mnogobroinite rodnini na meksikanskata si priiatelka Algre i doniak'de ot neia samata.
Stranitsa sled stranitsa vzaimootnosheniiata mezhdu vsichki tiakh se razvivat i promeniat, kakto i predstavite im edin za drug. V tipichniia si stil Shafak preplita ost'r khumor s pronitsatelni nabliudeniia, za da s'zdade p'st'r vodov'rtezh ot liubov i priiatelstvo, izgnanie i prinadlezhnost, Iztok i Zapad, koito se razgr'shcha na fona na s'vremenna Amerika. Avtorkata opisva neinoto bogatstvo i mnogoobrazie ot kulturi, bez da prem'lchava za drugata strana na medala - zagubata na sobstvenata identichnost."	�G�z@"	�G�z@"	)\���(@"	)\���(@"	=
